@title STORY • JAYDEN: SINCE WE WERE SIX
@bg harris_house_day
You're Jayden Harris. Thanksgiving break, freshman year, flashback. The Harris kitchen. Your mom Diana and Vega Sterling are laughing so hard they're crying over a pie.
And Paris is at the table, six years old in your memory and nineteen in real life, both at once. She's been at every holiday you can remember.
Diana: Jayden. Stop staring at that girl and carry these plates.
Jayden: I'm not staring.
Diana: You've been staring since kindergarten, baby.
@bg track_stadium_day
Present day. You're dating Suki. Suki is funny and loud and everybody loves her. You do too. Just not the way you're supposed to.
@show suki
Suki: You coming to the party Friday?
Jayden: Yeah. Of course.
She smiles. Then she looks past you, at the long jump pit. At Jamal. You notice. You don't say anything. Neither of you ever says anything.
> [Good] Take Suki's hand. Try harder. -> a1
> [Bold] "Suki... are we okay?" -> a2
> [Bad] Look for Paris in the sprint group instead. -> a3
*a1
@add Suki_Effort 2
You try. You really do. It feels like running the 100 in boots.
@jump a_done
*a2
@add Honesty 2
Suki: (too fast) We're fine! Why? Are you not fine?
Jayden: I'm fine.
Two people saying "fine" in a row. Both lying.
@jump a_done
*a3
@add Paris_Heart 2
@add Guilt 1
She's laughing at something Alexa said. She doesn't see you looking. She never does. You've gotten good at it.
*a_done
@bg dorm_room_night
@show jamal
Jamal is your roommate and your relay partner and the best person you know. Tonight he can't look you in the eye.
Jamal: Jay. Can I ask you something weird?
Jayden: Always.
Jamal: If you knew something that would hurt your boy... but it might be the best thing for him in the long run... would you want to know?
> [Good] "Always tell me the truth, man." -> b1
> [Sweet] "Is this about Suki?" -> b2
> [Bitchy] "That's way too deep for 1 a.m., bro." -> b3
*b1
@add Honesty 3
Jamal: (long breath) ...Not tonight. Soon. I promise.
He means it. You trust him. That's going to matter later.
@jump end
*b2
@add Honesty 2
Jamal goes completely still. That's all the answer you need. You're surprised by how little it hurts. You're surprised it mostly feels like relief.
@jump end
*b3
Jamal: (laughing, relieved) Yeah. Yeah, you're right. Goodnight, Jay.
He doesn't sleep. You can hear him not sleeping.
*end
Jayden Harris is everybody's favorite. He's been trying for a year to be the right boyfriend for the wrong girl. The right girl has been at his kitchen table since they were six.
